equest our report.\",\"date\":\"2026-06-10\"},\"title\":\"HackMD is now SOC 2 Type II compliant: Security you can trust\",\"content\":\"$33\",\"date\":{\"year\":\"2026\",\"month\":\"06\",\"day\":\"10\"},\"slug\":\"hackmd-soc2-2026\",\"tags\":[\"en\",\"company\"],\"author\":\"$6:2:1:props:posts:0:author\",\"publishedAt\":\"2026-06-10T12:47:05.470Z\",\"hashedKey\":\"ws4DC\"},{\"id\":\"OBHjx_a_Qf22Hzhz7biaJw\",\"meta\":{\"title\":\"Best Markdown Editors for Your Agents in 2026\",\"tags\":\"en, education\",\"description\":\"A comparison of five Markdown platforms built for AI agent workflows in 2026, evaluated on API access, CLI tooling, MCP support, and content negotiation, with honest tradeoffs.\",\"image\":\"https://hackmd.io/_uploads/HyHP-k0gfl.jpg\",\"author\":\"ChaseHack\",\"summary\":\"As AI agents increasingly read, write, and manage documentation, this guide compares five platforms, HackMD, GitBook, Mintlify, Notion, and ReadMe, on the capabilities that matter for agentic workflows such as programmatic access, CLI tooling, MCP servers, and Markdown-native delivery, with the real tradeoffs of each.\",\"date\":\"2026-06-03\"},\"title\":\"Best Markdown Editors for Your Agents in 2026\",\"content\":\"$34\",\"date\":{\"year\":\"2026\",\"month\":\"06\",\"day\":\"03\"},\"slug\":\"best-markdown-editor-2026\",\"tags\":[\"en\",\"education\"],\"author\":\"$6:2:1:props:posts:0:author\",\"publishedAt\":\"2026-06-03T17:17:19.425Z\",\"hashedKey\":\"Z1Tx0NX\"},{\"id\":\"ij6Tbns1QdWVW7R80wFCjg\",\"meta\":{\"title\":\"Improved PDF Export: A more reliable way to take your notes offline\",\"tags\":\"en, product\",\"description\":\"Export HackMD notes to PDF with more confidence. Get reliable conversion, better layout quality, and configurable export options.\",\"image\":\"https://hackmd.io/_uploads/S19BFCuJzx.jpg\",\"author\":\"ChaseHack\",\"summary\":\"Explore HackMD's improved PDF export experience. More reliable conversion, better output quality, and new layout controls help you turn your notes into PDFs you can actually trust.\",\"date\":\"2026-05-18\"},\"title\":\"Improved PDF Export: A more reliable way to take your notes offline\",\"content\":\"$35\",\"date\":{\"year\":\"2026\",\"month\":\"05\",\"day\":\"18\"},\"slug\":\"hackmd-improved-pdf\",\"tags\":[\"en\",\"product\"],\"author\":\"$6:2:1:props:posts:0:author\",\"publishedAt\":\"2026-05-18T18:24:36.169Z\",\"hashedKey\":\"dA69N\"},{\"id\":\"herk02tdTjKwOy2mZDdLpA\",\"meta\":{\"title\":\"Upload Markdown Files: A faster way to bring your content into HackMD\",\"tags\":\"en, product\",\"description\":\"Upload single or multiple Markdown files to HackMD directly from Overview. Supports .md, .markdown, .mdown, .mkd, and .txt\",\"image\":\"https://hackmd.io/_uploads/HkKGRgS6bl.jpg\",\"author\":\"ChaseHack\",\"summary\":\"Explore HackMD's new Markdown file upload in Overview. Upload one or many `.md` files at once and move your existing Markdown content into HackMD without the one-file-at-a-time slog.\",\"date\":\"2026-05-11\"},\"title\":\"Upload Markdown Files: A faster way to bring your content into HackMD\",\"content\":\"$36\",\"date\":{\"year\":\"2026\",\"month\":\"05\",\"day\":\"11\"},\"slug\":\"upload-markdown-hackmd\",\"tags\":[\"en\",\"product\"],\"author\":\"$6:2:1:props:posts:0:author\",\"publishedAt\":\"2026-05-11T14:28:50.464Z\",\"hashedKey\":\"Z6V0js\"},{\"id\":\"c60r0bQxRX-AzY5Af6jvBQ\",\"meta\":{\"title\":\"How Stoffel Labs Uses HackMD as the Governance Layer for AI-Generated Docs\",\"tags\":\"en, use-case\",\"description\":\"See how Stoffel Labs uses HackMD to turn AI-generated PRDs and RFCs into shared, reviewable team knowledge using notes, Books, and inline comments.\",\"image\":\"https://hackmd.io/_uploads/HJW0lf9Abx.jpg\",\"author\":\"ChaseHack\",\"summary\":\"AI tools can draft PRDs, RFCs, and design rationale faster than teams can review them. Stoffel Labs and HashCloak founder Mikerah Quintyne-Collins shares the workflow her team uses to close that gap.\",\"date\":\"2026-05-07\"},\"title\":\"How Stoffel Labs Uses HackMD as the Governance Layer for AI-Generated Docs\",\"content\":\"$37\",\"date\":{\"year\":\"2026\",\"month\":\"05\",\"day\":\"07\"},\"slug\":\"hackmd-governance-layer-ai\",\"tags\":[\"en\",\"use-case\"],\"author\":\"$6:2:1:props:posts:0:author\",\"publishedAt\":\"2026-05-19T03:01:59.971Z\",\"hashedKey\":\"AgY0P\"},{\"id\":\"3jZ-vBdlRfeQPA5ECMn9Jw\",\"meta\":{\"title\":\"When Your AI Writes the Docs: A Governance Layer for Agent-Generated Markdown\",\"tags\":\"en, education\",\"description\":\"AI agents now produce Markdown at scale, from spec drafts to skill files to meeting notes. HackMD is the governance layer that makes that output reviewable, versioned, and safe to ship.\",\"image\":\"https://hackmd.io/_uploads/SkECGwIpWe.jpg\",\"author\":\"ChaseHack\",\"summary\":\"AI agents are generating Markdown faster than humans can read it. Spec drafts, skill files, meeting notes, architecture docs; all produced in seconds, all demanding human judgment before they enter a source of truth. This post argues that the missing piece in modern AI stacks is not another agent, but a governance layer for what agents write.\",\"date\":\"2026-04-22\"},\"title\":\"When Your AI Writes the Docs: A Governance Layer for Agent-Generated Markdown\",\"content\":\"$38\",\"date\":{\"year\":\"2026\",\"month\":\"04\",\"day\":\"22\"},\"slug\":\"AI-writes-your-docs-hackmd\",\"tags\":[\"en\",\"education\"],\"author\":\"$6:2:1:props:posts:0:author\",\"publishedAt\":\"2026-04-22T17:54:08.955Z\",\"hashedKey\":\"ZyelR7\"},{\"id\":\"nMEJ4EtXTNiQJjgmk-hJhQ\",\"meta\":{\"title\":\"Built for Agents: Markdown-Native Content Negotiation, CLI Workflows, and API integration\",\"tags\":\"en, education\",\"description\":\"HackMD now supports content negotiation for AI agents via the Accept header, alongside its CLI and API. Here is how HackMD fits into agentic workflows natively.\",\"image\":\"https://hackmd.io/_uploads/ryByb_T9bg.jpg\",\"author\":\"ChaseHack\",\"summary\":\"AI agents are reshaping how content is consumed on the web. HackMD is already Markdown-native, and now it is adding content negotiation via the HTTP Accept header so agents can request clean Markdown directly. Combined with the HackMD CLI and API, this makes HackMD a natural fit for agentic development workflows.\",\"date\":\"2026-03-22\"},\"title\":\"Built for Agents: Markdown-Native Content Negotiation, CLI Workflows, and API integration\",\"content\":\"$39\",\"date\":{\"year\":\"2026\",\"month\":\"03\",\"day\":\"22\"},\"slug\":\"agentic-workflow-2026\",\"tags\":[\"en\",\"education\"],\"author\":\"$6:2:1:props:posts:0:author\",\"publishedAt\":\"2026-03-22T13:36:12.051Z\",\"hashedKey\":\"Z1ev9pM\"},{\"id\":\"SOuNCCfsQ7W8dYIrMPJh6w\",\"meta\":{\"title\":\"How to Use the HackMD Extension: Enhancing your VSCode experience\",\"tags\":\"en, education, product\",\"description\":\"Set up the official HackMD VS Code extension to edit, sync, and manage your Markdown notes without leaving your code editor.\",\"image\":\"https://hackmd.io/_uploads/SJ3SSdVt-x.jpg\",\"author\":\"ChaseHack\",\"summary\":\"Your HackMD notes don't have to live in a browser tab. The official VS Code extension lets you edit, sync, and organize your Markdown notes right alongside your code. This guide walks you through every step, from generating your API token to seeing your notes populate in the sidebar.\",\"date\":\"2026-03-04\"},\"title\":\"How to Use the HackMD Extension: Enhancing your VSCode experience\",\"content\":\"$3a\",\"date\":{\"year\":\"2026\",\"month\":\"03\",\"day\":\"04\"},\"slug\":\"vscode-extension-hackmd\",\"tags\":[\"en\",\"education\",\"product\"],\"author\":\"$6:2:1:props:posts:0:author\",\"publishedAt\":\"2026-03-04T14:03:14.572Z\",\"hashedKey\":\"ZMipC8\"},{\"id\":\"ybgy-hSIREWRmo-RWyJKyw\",\"meta\":{\"title\":\"The History of Markdown: How Plain Text Took Over\",\"tags\":\"en, education\",\"description\":\"From a 2004 Perl script to the lingua franca of developer documentation. A look at how Markdown evolved, why it fractured into flavors, and how CommonMark brought it back together.\",\"image\":\"https://hackmd.io/_uploads/B1JvUX5v-l.jpg\",\"author\":\"ChaseHack\",\"summary\":\"Markdown started as one developer's frustration with writing HTML by hand. Two decades later, it's everywhere, from README files to real-time collaboration platforms. This post traces how Markdown grew, why so many flavors exist, and why CommonMark matters for the future of collaborative writing.\",\"date\":\"2026-02-11\"},\"title\":\"The History of Markdown: How Plain Text Took Over\",\"content\":\"$3b\",\"date\":{\"year\":\"2026\",\"month\":\"02\",\"day\":\"11\"},\"slug\":\"markdown-history\",\"tags\":[\"en\",\"education\"],\"author\":\"$6:2:1:props:posts:0:author\",\"publishedAt\":\"2026-02-11T16:00:26.814Z\",\"hashedKey\":\"Z12xbdJ\"},{\"id\":\"WAHV9_kuRBm1RiuZaj0Y1Q\",\"meta\":{\"title\":\"Choosing a CMS for Technical Teams in 2026: Git‑Based vs. Headless vs. Collaborative Markdown\",\"tags\":\"en, education\",\"description\":\"This guide breaks down Git-based, headless, and collaborative Markdown CMS options with honest tradeoffs to help you choose the right architecture for how your team actually works.\",\"image\":\"https://hackmd.io/_uploads/BkCkcTePWg.jpg\",\"author\":\"ChaseHack\",\"summary\":\"Technical teams now manage living docs, developer portals, and multi-channel content that feeds websites, APIs, and AI systems simultaneously. This guide compares Git-based, headless, and collaborative Markdown CMS options with honest tradeoffs.\",\"date\":\"2026-02-04\"},\"title\":\"Choosing a CMS for Technical Teams in 2026: Git‑Based vs. Headless vs. Collaborative Markdown\",\"content\":\"$3c\",\"date\":{\"year\":\"2026\",\"month\":\"02\",\"day\":\"04\"},\"slug\":\"tech-teams-cms-2026\",\"tags\":[\"en\",\"education\"],\"author\":\"$6:2:1:props:posts:0:author\",\"publishedAt\":\"2026-02-04T13:59:39.697Z\",\"hashedKey\":\"1ox2t6\"},{\"id\":\